   "fields": [
    {
     "offset": 0,
     "type": "RSceneObj_vtbl *",
     "name": "vtable",
     "comment": "high: ctor stores 0x191be0; PS2 keeps its vptr at the END (+0x3c, ctor sw vtable_RSceneObj,0x3c), which is why every PS2 field sits 4 bytes lower than Xbox"
    },
    {
     "offset": 4,
     "type": "RSceneObj *",
     "name": "next",
     "comment": "high: SetMapNode/UseInstanceList/~RSceneObj: doubly linked list headed at MapNode+4, new obj inserted at head (next=old head); DestroySceneObjectList/InitializeSceneObjectListLighting walk +4; dtor poisons it 0xabababab. PS2 +0x0"
    },
    {
     "offset": 8,
     "type": "RSceneObj *",
     "name": "prev",
     "comment": "high: SetMapNode clears it on insert and fixes next->prev (+8); dtor unlinks via +4/+8. PS2 +0x4"
    },
    {
     "offset": 12,
     "type": "CARP::Instance *",
     "name": "sourceInstance",
     "comment": "high: POINTER, not a copy: ctor stores its CARP::Instance& arg (param_1_00[3]=param_1) and only copies it to a stack MATRIX4. 64-byte record: rows 0-3 are the transform, word +0x3c packs the bounding radius ((v&0x3ff)*table[bit30], bit31=compute), by"
    },
    {
     "offset": 16,
     "type": "CARP::BaseDesc *",
     "name": "baseDesc",
     "comment": "high: PS2 GetBaseDesc returns PS2 +0xc. Set in UseInstanceList from *(article+0x1c); *baseDesc is the model UGroup (SetVariation/GetViewDrawList/GetNumBones/GetBoneIndex/Reset); +4 flags (0x2000 = skip lighting), +0x10/+0x20 bbox min/max (GetBounding"
    },
    {
     "offset": 20,
     "type": "RCARPFile *",
     "name": "carpFile",
     "comment": "high: PS2 GetCARPFile returns PS2 +0x10. Load stores the URefCounter<RCARPFile> reference here; ~RSceneObj/Load RemoveReference it and FastFree(..,0x38)"
    },
    {
     "offset": 24,
     "type": "CARP::MapNode *",
     "name": "mapNode",
     "comment": "high: SetMapNode(CARP::MapNode*) stores its arg here after unlinking from the old node; UpdatePosition passes it to WTree::FindNode as the search start; UseInstanceList sets it to the world-tree root when flags bit2. PS2 +0x14 (SetMapNode)"
    },
    {
     "offset": 28,
     "type": "byte",
     "name": "renderTypeIndex",
     "comment": "medium: ctor zeroes it; no Xbox RSceneObj method reads it. PS2 GetRenderTypeIndex/SetRenderTypeIndex = lbu/sb PS2 +0x18 (byte 0 of the PS2 bitfield word at +0x18)"
    },
    {
     "offset": 29,
     "type": "byte",
     "name": "variation",
     "comment": "high: SetVariation stores (char)arg on success; Reset passes it to UseArticle; UseArticle writes it. PS2 GetVariation = lbu PS2 +0x19"
    },
    {
     "offset": 30,
     "type": "byte",
     "name": "brightness",
     "comment": "high: ctor sets 100. PS2 Brightness() = lbu PS2 +0x1a * (1/255); SetBrightness(float) clamps 0..1, *255, sb PS2 +0x1a; PS2 ctor also sb 100 there"
    },
    {
     "offset": 31,
     "type": "byte",
     "name": "flags",
     "comment": "high: Show/Hide bit0; ctor does &0xe1|1 (clears bits1-4, sets visible). On PS2 these are bits 24-28 of the word at PS2 +0x18 (Show/Hide = or/and 0x01000000, IsVisible = lb +0x1b &1)"
    },
    {
     "offset": 32,
     "type": "ushort",
     "name": "damagedZones",
     "comment": "medium: PS2 GetDamagedZones = lhu PS2 +0x1c. TriggerFX type 10 feeds the newly set bits to RAnimEngine::Handle::ProcessStimuliZones(0x12,..) and stores the mask; RenderEffects skips an effect whose zone (effect byte +0x16) bit is set here unless the "
    },
    {
     "offset": 34,
     "type": "ushort",
     "name": "damageEffectZones",
     "comment": "low: TriggerFX type 9: if new bits, DamageEffects(this+0x22 | mask) then ORs mask in; UseInstanceList zeroes it. PS2 +0x1e (TriggerFX uses it the same way); no PS2 accessor, name invented"
    },
    {
     "offset": 36,
     "type": "uint",
     "name": "effectDecayTime",
     "comment": "medium: TriggerEffects/DamageEffects/DecayEffects set it to frame counter DAT_001f2a4c+600 while any effect is active, 0 otherwise; RenderEffects calls DecayEffects once the counter passes it. PS2 +0x20 (RenderEffects field9_0x20). Name invented"
    },
    {
     "offset": 40,
     "type": "PhysicsObject *",
     "name": "physics",
     "comment": "high: SetPhysics(PhysicsObject*) stores here; PS2 GetPhysics (both overloads) = lw PS2 +0x24. UpdatePosition/GetVelocity/SetTransform/EnableTarget/SetEventDynamicData read +0x48 bit0 (simple body) and short +0x4a (rigid body index)"
    },
    {
     "offset": 44,
     "type": "RAnimEngine::Handle *",
     "name": "animHandle",
     "comment": "high: UseInstanceList stores RAnimEngine::Handle::Create(...); dtor/Load/UseInstanceList Stop and operator_delete(..,0x40). The effect state lives in the handle: effects array +0x14, zone-mask ushort array +0x18, instance count byte +0x1c, numEffects"
    },
    {
     "offset": 48,
     "type": "RPathEngine::RPathHandle *",
     "name": "pathHandle",
     "comment": "high: ctor stores RPathEngine::GetPathHandle(instance); GetVelocity returns pathHandle+0x88 when there is no physics. PS2 GetPathHandle = lw PS2 +0x2c"
    },
    {
     "offset": 52,
     "type": "WTargetable *",
     "name": "target",
     "comment": "high: EnableTarget FastAlloc(0x50,'WTargetable') and stores it; SetPhysics/~RSceneObj RemoveReference and clear it. PS2 +0x30 (DisableTarget clears PS2 +0x30)"
    },
    {
     "offset": 56,
     "type": "SceneObjCollisionInfo *",
     "name": "collisionInfo",
     "comment": "medium: AddCollisionInfo lazily __builtin_new(0x20)s it: {COORD3 pointSum; uint frame; COORD3 normalSum; uint count}; GetCollisionInfo averages it for the current frame or deletes it; dtor/UseInstanceList delete it. PS2 +0x34. Struct type name invent"
    },
    {
     "offset": 60,
     "type": "char *",
     "name": "name",
     "comment": "medium: UseInstanceList stores its name arg or '<<unknown>>' (UseInstance passes '<<fragment1>>', UseArticle the article's 'Name' tag). PS2 +0x38 (UseInstanceList piVar5[0xe]). No accessor; debug name"
    }
   ],
