     "type": "RSceneObj",
     "name": "super_RSceneObj"
    },
    {
     "offset": 64,
     "type": "float[12]",
     "name": "params",
     "comment": "high: ctor zeroes 12 dwords; SetProcAnimState calls SetProcAnimParamList(this+0x40,12). PS2 GetParam(i) = this+0x40+4*i (same offset on PS2)"
    },
    {
     "offset": 112,
     "type": "ulonglong",
     "name": "springEffectMask",
     "comment": "medium: PostLoad ORs 1<<i for every anim-handle effect of type 8; UpdatePosition walks its set bits and runs UpdateSpringMassSystem for each. PS2 sd zero,0x70 / PostLoad same. Name invented"
    },
    {
     "offset": 120,
     "type": "uint",
     "name": "numBones",
     "comment": "high: AllocateSkeleton stores the count; dtor frees bones with size numBones<<6. PS2 NumBones = lw +0x78"
    },
    {
     "offset": 124,
     "type": "MATRIX4 *",
     "name": "bones",
     "comment": "high: AllocateSkeleton FastAlloc(n*0x40,'Bones') and inits each to identity; SetProcAnimState passes (bones,numBones) to SetProcAnimXFormList; UpdatePosition writes bone[id-1]. PS2 GetBone(i) = *(+0x7c)+(i-1)*0x40"
    },
    {
     "offset": 128,
     "type": "COORD4",
     "name": "springPrevPos",
     "comment": "low: ctor sets (0,0,0,-1); UpdateSpringMassSystem treats w==-1 as 'uninitialised' (resets both to (0,0,0,1)), then shifts +0x90 into +0x80 each step. PS2 same offset. Name invented"
    },
    {
     "offset": 144,
     "type": "COORD4",
     "name": "springPos",
     "comment": "low: ctor (0,0,0,-1); UpdateSpringMassSystem stores the new spring point here after velocity from (+0x90 - +0x80). PS2 same offset. Name invented"
    }
   ],
